      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STAR MINERVA (3) is worth following up after a brave debut win at Kembla Grange. Jumps straight to Class 2, so there's obviously a stable rap. Has clear upside and can make it 2/2. WOLF ISLAND (4) is much more exposed but consistent nevertheless. Strips rock-hard fit off a head-win here last time and gets in well again with a 2kg apprentice on. OKAMI STAR (2) resumes and has been fitted with two quiet trials. Form is patchy but he shoulders peaks that can threaten. ZOE (8) was well below her best when resuming at Gosford and is open to sharp improvement with that run out of the way. Has been kept on the fresh side and rises to a more suitable trip.",
